*  s184 seat7 (row span-frame-flip): the SCRIP_SPAN_FRAME=1 SILENT WRONG ANSWER, minimal.
*  RED ARMED ONLY, nondeterministic (~8/12), both media; GREEN at default 12/12.
*  Ingredient that makes it bite: the charset is NOT constant-foldable (*CS is deferred),
*  so the SPAN's charset operand is staged on the flat zeta-SPINE and read as [rsp+120].
*  Arming re-homes the leaf cell to rbp and widens the MATCH_BEGIN carve by 16, which moves
*  rsp for the whole graph -- but no flat operand offset is rebased, so that read lands 16
*  bytes past its slot, in caller territory.  Wrong charset => SPAN matches nothing => the
*  |epsilon arm wins => RPOS(0) fails => the 'quoted' fallback.  Control: ctl_span_constcs_alt.
          epsilon        =
          CS             = '0123456789' &UCASE '_' &LCASE
          T              = 'Name'
          T              POS(0) ANY(&UCASE &LCASE) (SPAN(*CS) | epsilon) RPOS(0)   :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT         = 'bare'                                                  :(END)
NO        OUTPUT         = 'quoted'
END
